ICP ladder switched on 2026-10-21.

What this file does: the 08:30 first-touch job runs scripts/seed_icp_drafts.py --apply, which
composes the four-touch ICP sequence for leads whose lead_source is icp_research. While this
file was absent the script printed why and exited 0, so nothing was drafted.

The sequence, per touch:
  1  the sponsor-taking lists in the lead's lane, who is already buying in one, and for data
     and intelligence companies one sentence offering the same records through the REST API and
     the MCP server
  2  the reader profile behind the list touch one led on (and, for data companies, the API
     fields beside it)
  3  for data companies: the MCP tool count (17, verified against services/mcp/tools.js and
     .well-known/agent.json), the docs URL, the endpoint, and a trial key offer; for everyone
     else the other end of the lane
  4  the close, one tracked link attached, trial key and sample export for data companies

Composing only fills the pad queue. Nothing sends unless the 09:00 gate passes it, so this file
does not open a send path: it opens the drafting one.

Who is skipped at compose time: leads whose event log says "do not draft" (Hunter, the contact
supplier), and any lead whose address is a shared mailbox (the gate would hold it outright).
